hadiths[35]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1655","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I witnessed the alliance of al-Mutayyabin with my uncles when I was a boy, and I would not love to have red camels and to break it. al-Zuhri said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Islam did not meet an alliance but that it increased it in strength, and there is no alliance in Islam. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar."
"1656","Ibrahim ibn Sad told us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that he said to him: Umar said to him: O boy, have you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or from any of his companions, when a man doubts in his prayer what he should do. He said: And while he was so, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came. So he said: What are you discussing. Umar said: I asked this boy: Have you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or any of his companions, when a man doubts in his prayer what he should do. Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he prayed one or two, let him count it as one; and when he does not know whether he prayed two or three, let him count it as two; and when he does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him count it as three; then let him prostrate when he finishes his prayer while sitting, before giving salams, two prostrations."
"1657","Sufyan told us, from Amr: Bajalah heard saying: I was a scribe for Jaz ibn Muawiyah, uncle of al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, then the letter of Umar came to us a year before his death: Kill every magician, and Sufyan sometimes said: And sorceress, and separate every closely related couple of the Magians, and forbid them the zamzamah. So we killed three sorceresses, and we began separating a man from his close kinswoman according to the Book of Allah. And Jaz made much food and laid the sword on his thigh and invited the Magians, and they cast down a mule-load or two mule-loads of silver, and they ate without zamzamah. And Umar had not taken, and Sufyan sometimes said: Accepted, the jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf bore witness that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took it from the Magians of Hajar. And my father said: Sufyan said: Bajalah performed hajj with Musab in the year seventy."
"1658","Sufyan told us, from Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws: I heard Umar saying to Abd al-Rahman and Talhah and al-Zubayr and Sad: I adjure you by Allah by Whom the heaven and earth stand, and once he said: By Whose permission the heaven and earth stand, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. They said: O Allah, yes."
"1659","Yazid ibn Harun told us: Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, that his father narrated to him that he entered upon Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf while he was ill, and Abd al-Rahman said to him: Kinship has joined you; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am al-Rahman; I created the womb and split for it from My name. So whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever cuts it, I cut him; so cut it off, or he said: Whoever cuts it off, I cut him off."
"1660","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, told us: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl told us: al-Nadr ibn Shayban told us, he said: I met Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman. I said: Narrate to me something you heard from your father, which he heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the month of Ramadan. He said: Yes; my father narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, obligated the fasting of Ramadan, and I legislated its standing in prayer. So whoever fasts it and stands it in faith, he emerges from sins as on the day his mother bore him."
"1661","Yahya ibn Ishaq told us: Ibn Lahiah told us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, that Ibn Qariz informed him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a woman prays her five, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, it is said to her: Enter Paradise from whichever gates of Paradise you wish."
"1662","Abu Salamah Mansur ibn Salamah al-Khuzai told us: Layth told us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and I followed him until he entered a palm grove, then he prostrated and prolonged the prostration until I feared, or I dreaded, that Allah had taken him or seized him. He said: So I came to look, and he raised his head and said: What is the matter with you, O Abd al-Rahman. He said: So I mentioned that to him, and he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Shall I not give you glad tidings; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to you: Whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you, I send peace upon him."
"1663","Yunus told us: Layth told us, from Yazid, from Amr, from Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I entered the mosque and saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, coming out of the mosque, so I followed him and he mentioned the hadith."
"1664","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, told us: Sulayman ibn Bilal told us: Amr ibn Abi Amr told us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and headed toward his charity land, then he entered and faced the qiblah and fell prostrating, and he prolonged the prostration until I thought Allah, Mighty and Majestic, had seized his soul therein. So I drew near to him and sat, then he raised his head and said: Who is this. I said: Abd al-Rahman. He said: What is your concern. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you prostrated a prostration and I feared Allah, Mighty and Majestic, had seized your soul therein. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and gave me glad tidings, and said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you, I send peace upon him. So I prostrated to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in thanks."
"1665","Haytham ibn Kharijah told us; Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning Abdullah, said: And I myself heard it from al-Haytham ibn Kharijah: Rishdin told us, from Abdullah ibn al-Walid, that he heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his father that he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went for his need, and the time of prayer overtook them, so they established the prayer and Abd al-Rahman led them. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and prayed with the people behind him one rakah, and when he gave salams he said: You did right, or you did well."
"1666","Rawh told us: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah told us: al-Zuhri told us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When the epidemic is in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it, and when it is in a land and you are in it, do not leave it."
"1667","Aswad ibn Amir told us: Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that a group of Arabs came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Madinah and accepted Islam, and the epidemic of Madinah, its fever, afflicted them, so they relapsed and left Madinah. Then a group of his companions, meaning the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met them and said to them: What is the matter with you that you returned. They said: The epidemic of Madinah afflicted us and we disliked Madinah. They said: Do you not have in the Messenger of Allah an example. Then some of them said: They became hypocrites, and some of them said: They did not become hypocrites; they are Muslims. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: What is the matter with you concerning the hypocrites in two parties, and Allah cast them back for what they earned, the verse."
"1668","Hashim ibn al-Qasim told us: Sharik told us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the voice of Ibn al-Mughtarif, or Ibn al-Gharf, the camel-driver in the depth of the night while we were heading to Makkah, so Umar quickened his mount until he joined the people, and he was with Abd al-Rahman. When dawn broke Umar said: Now be quiet; now dawn has broken; remember Allah. He said: Then he saw khuffs on Abd al-Rahman. He said: And two khuffs. He said: I wore them with one who is better than you, or with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Umar said: I adjure you to take them off, for I fear people will look at you and follow you."
"1669","He said: And Ishaq ibn Isa narrated it to us: Sharik told us and he mentioned it with its chain, and he said: I wore them with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1670","Affan told us: Hammad ibn Salamah told us: Hisham ibn Urwah told us, from Urwah, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted me and Umar ibn al-Khattab land of such and such. Then al-Zubayr went to the family of Umar and bought their share from them, then he came to Uthman ibn Affan and said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf claims the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted him and Umar ibn al-Khattab land of such and such, and I bought the share of the family of Umar. Uthman said: Abd al-Rahman is acceptable in testimony for him and against him."
"1671","al-Hakam ibn Nafi told us: Ismail ibn Ayyash told us, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, referring it to Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Ibn al-Sadi, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Emigration does not cease as long as the enemy is fought. Then Muawiyah and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Emigration is two traits: one is that you abandon evil deeds, and the other is that you emigrate to Allah and His Messenger. And emigration does not cease as long as repentance is accepted, and repentance keeps being accepted until the sun rises from the west. When it rises, every heart is sealed with what is in it, and people are spared deeds."
"1672","Abu al-Mughirah told us: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz told us: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: When the Magian came out from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I asked him, and he informed me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him the choice between the jizyah and killing, so he chose the jizyah."
"1673","Abu Salamah Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Majishun told us, from Salih ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he said: I was standing on the day of Badr in the row, looking to my right and to my left, and I was between two boys of the Ansar young in age; I wished I were between sturdier ribs than theirs. Then one of them nudged me and said: O uncle, do you know Abu Jahl. He said: I said: Yes, and what is your need, O son of my brother. He said: It reached me that he reviled the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if I saw him my darkness would not leave his darkness until the sooner of us dies. He said: Then the other nudged me and said to me the like of it. He said: So I marveled at that. He said: And I had barely waited before I looked at Abu Jahl pacing among the people, and I said to them: Do you not see; this is your man whom you ask about. So they rushed at him and faced them, and they struck him until they killed him. Then they returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. He said: Which of you killed him. Each one of them said: I killed him. He said: Have you wiped your swords. They said: No. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked at the two swords and said: Both of you killed him. And he awarded his spoils to Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh; and they are Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh and Muadh ibn Afra."
"1674","Affan told us: Abu Awanah told us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, he said: The storyteller of the people of Filastin narrated to me, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three things, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if I were to swear upon them: Wealth does not decrease from charity, so give charity; and no servant pardons an injustice seeking thereby the Face of Allah except that Allah raises him thereby; and Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, said: Except that Allah increases him thereby in honor on the Day of Resurrection; and no servant opens a door of begging except that Allah opens upon him a door of poverty."
"1675","Qutaybah ibn Said told us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas is in Paradise, and Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl is in Paradise, and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah is in Paradise."
"1676","Ismail told us: Ibn Ishaq, meaning Abd al-Rahman, told us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I witnessed as a boy with my uncles the alliance of al-Mutayyabin, and I would not love to have red camels and to break it."
"1677","Ismail told us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq told us: Makhul narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays and doubts in his prayer, if he doubts between one and two let him count them as one, and if he doubts between two and three let him count them as two, and if he doubts between three and four let him count them as three, until the doubt is about addition; then let him prostrate two prostrations before giving salams, then give salams. Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: And Husayn ibn Abdullah said to me: Did he narrate it to you with a chain. I said: No. He said: But he narrated to me that Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I sat with Umar ibn al-Khattab and he said: O Ibn Abbas, when a man is confused in his prayer and does not know whether he added or decreased. I said: By Allah, O Commander of the Believers, I do not know that I heard anything about that. Umar said: By Allah, I do not know. He said: And while we were so, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came and said: What is this you are discussing. Umar said to him: We mentioned a man doubting in his prayer, what he should do. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying this hadith."
"1678","Hajjaj and Yazid, the meaning, said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed Umar ibn al-Khattab while he was traveling on the road to Syria, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: This ailment punished the nations before you with it; so when you hear of it in a land do not enter upon it, and when it occurs in a land and you are in it do not leave fleeing from it. He said: So Umar ibn al-Khattab returned from Syria."
"1679","Abd al-Razzaq told us: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab went out intending Syria and he mentioned the hadith. He said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was absent, then he came and said: I have knowledge of this; I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When you hear of it in a land do not come upon it, and when it occurs in a land and you are in it do not leave fleeing from it."
"1680","Abd al-Razzaq told us: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Abu al-Raddad al-Laythi informed him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am al-Rahman; I created the womb and split for it a name from My name. So whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever cuts it, I cut him off."
"1681","Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah told us: My father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Abu al-Raddad al-Laythi informed him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am al-Rahman, and I created the womb and derived for it from My name. So whoever joins it, Allah joins him, and whoever cuts it, I cut him off."
"1682","Ishaq ibn Isa told us: Malik informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to Syria, and when he came to Sargh it reached him that the epidemic had occurred in Syria. Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you hear of it in a land do not come upon it, and when it occurs in a land and you are in it do not leave fleeing from it. So Umar ibn al-Khattab returned from Sargh."
"1683","Ishaq ibn Isa told us: Malik informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to Syria until when he was at Sargh the commanders of the troops, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and his companions, met him and informed him that the epidemic had occurred in Syria, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came, and he had been away attending to some need, and said: I have knowledge of this; I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When it is in a land and you are in it do not leave fleeing from it, and when you hear of it in a land do not come upon it. He said: So Umar praised Allah then turned back."
"1684","Abu al-Ala al-Hasan ibn Sawwar told us: Hisham ibn Sad told us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When you hear of it in a land and you are not in it do not enter it, and when it occurs and you are in it do not leave fleeing from it."
"1685","Abd al-Razzaq told us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Bajalah al-Tamimi, he said: Umar did not want to take the jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf bore witness that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took it from the Magians of Hajar."
"1686","Sufyan told us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, he said: Abu al-Raddad complained of illness, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf visited him. Abu al-Raddad said: The best of them and most joining of them as I know is Abu Muhammad. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am Allah and I am al-Rahman; I created the womb and split for it from My name. So whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever cuts it, I cut him off."
"1687","Yazid ibn Harun told us: Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, that his father narrated to him that he entered upon Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf while he was ill, and Abd al-Rahman said to him: Kinship has joined you; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am al-Rahman, and I created the womb and split for it from My name. So whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever cuts it, I cut him; or he said: Whoever cuts it off, I cut him off."
"1688","Surayj ibn al-Numan told us: Nuh ibn Qays told us, from Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami, from al-Nadr ibn Shayban al-Huddani, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I said to him: Will you not narrate to me a hadith from your father which your father heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said to him: Ramadan came, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ramadan is a month in which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, obligated its fasting, and I legislated for the Muslims its standing in prayer. So whoever fasts it with faith and seeking reward emerges from sins as on the day his mother bore him."
"1689","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan ibn Malik said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting: Muhammad ibn Yazid told us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to discuss the matter of prayer with Umar, then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to them and said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They said: Yes. He said: So I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever prays a prayer doubting about deficiency, let him pray until he doubts about addition. This is the end of the hadiths of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him."
